course: dictionary
lesson: 10880
title: Villains and the hero
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A villain is the bad character in a story, play or film. They do evil things and fight against the hero. When you meet a villain, look for the hero and see who is working against them.
explain: Villain can also mean a person who does wrong or harmful things, such as a criminal. Context shows which meaning fits: in a story it is the baddie, and in a sentence about a crime it is the criminal.
explain: Be careful not to use the word unfairly. «Ghost stories and playground legends are fun, but they should not turn a real neighbour into a villain.» A real person is not a villain just because a story says so.
explain: Everyday talk has a trap. «The villain of the piece» means the one to blame. Read the whole scene to find out which meaning the writer means.
fact: A villain is a bad character in a story, play or film, who fights against the hero.
fact: Villain can also mean a person who does wrong or harmful things, such as a criminal.
fact: Villain is a noun: one villain, many villains.
fact: «Real red foxes are not sly villains: they are careful, curious animals that learn fast and eat almost anything.»
fact: In the cartoon Madagascar, «a fossa pack is a gang of villains», but the real fossa is a lone hunter related to mongooses.
exercise: «The hero beat the villain at the end of the story.» What is a villain? | A kind helper who saves the day | The main good character in the story | A person who reads the story aloud | *A bad character who fights against the hero
exercise: Mia says the real red fox is a villain because it is sly. What does the text say about real red foxes? | They only live in the Arctic | *They are careful, curious animals that learn fast | They are lemurs led by females | They are sly villains that steal from every farm
exercise: «Vultures are not villains.» What does this sentence tell you? | Vultures are the best villains in films | *Vultures are not bad characters or wicked creatures | Vultures are the main hero of the story | Vultures live in Madagascar
test: «Ghost stories should not turn a real neighbour into a villain.» Which idea is this sentence about? | Ghost stories are always true | Playground games are for heroes only | *Real people should not be called villains just because of a story | Neighbours always live next to a villain
test: Ellie reads «the villain of the piece» in a newspaper about a bank robbery. What does it mean? | A small, quiet animal | The best character in the story | *The one to blame | A park keeper
exam: Which meaning of «bit the dust» fits a villain: died or broke down? | Found a dust bin | *Died | Broke down | Moved very fast
